   "notes": "18-19 Sidney St: neo-Georgian/Edwardian red brick with heavy stone dressings: stone window architraves with keystones, first-floor window on the north bay has a pedimented stone surround and a wrought-iron balconette, stone band courses and a stone cornice. Cream stone ground-floor surround with signboard fascia (was Jack Wills in the photo; no current OSM POI, fascia_text blank). 4 bays estimated over 11.1 m; 'Sidney Street' nameplate on the north pier."
